{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_EIYfgHy40nVoJuGdgVZ1tU9G","content":"1\t# stories-api\n2\t\n3\tA small story library behind `POST /stories` (Lambda + DynamoDB table `stories`,\n4\tpartition key `slug`). `src/app.py` is the whole service: `handler()` parses\n5\tthe request and `publish()` stores the story together with its three most\n6\tsimilar existing stories (`similar: [{slug, score}]`), so the reader page can\n7\tshow \"related\" without any query at read time. `logs/error.log` is the\n8\tproduction log from the first two publishes after the deploy.\n9\t\n10\tTests use an in-memory table (`tests/fake_dynamo.py`) that validates items the\n11\tway boto3 does, so no AWS account is needed. Run them with\n12\t`python3 -m unittest discover tests` from the repo root."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_YIybid56tOUiiel3Yw8wYpoz","content":"1\timport os\n2\timport sys\n3\timport unittest\n4\t\n5\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"src\"))\n6\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(__file__))\n7\t\n8\timport app  # noqa: E402\n9\tfrom fake_dynamo import FakeTable  # noqa: E402\n10\t\n11\t\n12\tclass PublishTest(unittest.TestCase):\n13\t    def test_publish_stores_story(self):\n14\t        table = FakeTable()\n15\t        story = {\n16\t            \"slug\": \"why-my-cron-ran-twice\",\n17\t            \"title\": \"Why my cron ran twice\",\n18\t            \"tags\": [\"cron\", \"linux\"],\n19\t            \"body\": \"Two crontabs, one for root and one for me, both had the line.\",\n20\t        }\n21\t        stored = app.publish(table, story)\n22\t        self.assertEqual(stored[\"slug\"], \"why-my-cron-ran-twice\")\n23\t        self.assertEqual(table.get_item(Key={\"slug\": \"why-my-cron-ran-twice\"})[\"Item\"][\"title\"], \"Why my cron ran twice\")\n24\t        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 1)\n25\t\n26\t\n27\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n28\t    unittest.main()"}
